# File: scripts/__tests__/publish-approved-spec.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/619-create-the-spec-directory-in-publish-approved-spec-prepare/requirements.md
Feature: Create the spec directory in publish-approved-spec prepare

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: prepare creates the spec directory
    Given a repository whose default branch has no "specs/42-add-x/"
    When "prepare --issue 42 --name 42-add-x" succeeds
    Then the returned "specDir" exists as a directory
    And the JSON output has the fields "ok", "branch", "worktree", "specDir" and "created" with their current values

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Reuse leaves existing spec files untouched
    Given a spec worktree for "42-add-x" whose "specDir" already holds the four spec files
    When "prepare --issue 42 --name 42-add-x" runs again
    Then it succeeds with the same "branch", "worktree" and "specDir" and "created" false
    And the content of every existing spec file is unchanged

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario Outline: The workflow states that specDir exists
    Given the file "<file>"
    When its description of the "prepare" output is read
    Then it states that "specDir" exists after "prepare" succeeds

    Examples:
      | file                                       |
      | workflows/write-spec/WORKFLOW.md           |
      | workflows/write-spec/references/publish.md |
